## 3. Key finding of this batch (C-31)
Literal independent detection of SF2 (variant A1) contradicts the soft allowance of §13.6: the adapter returns empty text for every HTTP error, timeout and transport exception, and "no candidate" is empty by construction, so every such call would become SF1+SF2 or SF4+SF2 and fail the round; `f_S` = 1 could never be used. Measured with an in-memory patch: 10 tests flip (8 older + 2 pinned). The earlier recommendation "detect every flag independently" was withdrawn in `MASTER_PROPOSED_DECISION_RECORD.md`. Until the owner/advisor choose A1, A2 (SF2 only for a received 2xx response) or B (keep precedence, record it), the current code lets an HTTP 503 with an empty body PASS within `f_S` = 1, which differs from the literal reading of spec 810. **This is the main rule point to settle before any pilot call.**

